// f018_boot_block_limit.fl -- boot's PER-BLOCK DIRECT STATEMENT CEILING (512) pinned as a permanent probe.
//
// THE CEILING UNDER TEST (boot end only) -- MEASURED 2026-10-15, not read off a comment:
//   boot\lib_parse.fl parse_block() buffers a block's DIRECT child statements in `int tmp[512];`
//   and returns -101 the moment a 512th direct statement is reached (the 512-slot buffer is
//   already full at that point -- the guard fires one early):
//       int tmp[512];  ...  if (cnt >= 512) return -101;
//   b1_emit then prints `parse err=-101 ...` + `compile FAIL err=2`, and the boot compiler
//   process exits 12.  The real compiler (flint.exe) has no such ceiling.
//   MEASURED boundary on main's body (x-statements + the trailing `return x;`):
//       510 x-stmts (511 children) -> boot compiles, program exits 510
//       511 x-stmts (512 children) -> boot refuses, err=-101 at the `return` token
//   So the ceiling is 512 DIRECT CHILDREN per block, i.e. 511 usable statements when a
//   `return` shares the block.  Note it is DIRECT children only: wrapping statements in a
//   nested block resets the count (that is how gen-srclimit.ps1 pushes ~20000 statements
//   through boot).
//   This is a LOUD FAILURE, but since it surfaces as an ERROR CODE it is easy to mis-file as
//   a defect.  Pinned here so that it can never degrade into silence (compiles "fine" yet
//   emits a wrong binary) and so that a moved threshold turns the ledger row red.
//
// SHAPE: ONE block (main's body) holding 513 direct `x = x + 1;` statements -- the file is
//   a few KB, nowhere near the 262144-byte SOURCE ceiling (that one is pinned separately by
//   gen-srclimit.ps1, which generates an oversized source under %TEMP%).
//
// PAIRING: f018_boot_block_limit.fl (513 statements: boot MUST refuse) and
//   f018b_boot_block_limit_ok.fl (510 statements = 511 children: boot MUST still compile and
//   run) pin the threshold from both sides; either one moving alone turns its own row red.
//
// EXPECTED (computed, never hand-typed -- see the generator tail below):
//   flint.exe        : compiles; the program exits with the statement count
//   boot\b1_emit.exe : refuses (parse err=-101, compile FAIL err=2, process exit 12)
//                      => facts-run.ps1 -Compiler boot exits 1
//   NOTE: 513 x-statements = 514 direct children in main -- over the 512 ceiling by 2, so this
//   file is not sitting exactly on the edge.  Exactness is f018b's job (510 x-stmts = 511
//   children, the largest shape boot still accepts) -- f018's job is to be unambiguously over.
//
// REGENERATE (pure ASCII, no BOM) -- the trailing two lines COMPUTE the expected values:
//   $sb = New-Object System.Text.StringBuilder
//   [void]$sb.Append("int main() {`n  int x = 0;`n")
//   for ($i = 0; $i -lt 513; $i++) { [void]$sb.Append("  x = x + 1;`n") }
//   [void]$sb.Append("  return x;`n}`n")
//   [IO.File]::WriteAllText("E:\FLINT-lab\test\facts\f018_boot_block_limit.fl", $sb.ToString(), (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)))
//   $b = [IO.File]::ReadAllBytes("E:\FLINT-lab\test\facts\f018_boot_block_limit.fl"); "stmts=513 bytes=$($b.Length) exit=513 ascii_gt127=$(($b | Where-Object { $_ -gt 127 }).Count)"
